P(X = k) = \binom{10}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10}
\] To find the probability of getting at least 8 heads, we need to sum the probabilities of getting exactly 8, 9, and 10 heads. \[
P(X \geq 8) = P(X = 8) + P(X = 9) + P(X = 10)
\] Using the binomial probability formula, we can calculate these probabilities. \[
P(X = 8) = \binom{10}{8} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} = \frac{45}{1024}
\] \[
P(X = 9) = \binom{10}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} = \frac{10}{1024}
\] \[
P(X = 10) = \binom{10}{10} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} = \frac{1}{1024}
\] Summing these probabilities, we get \[
P(X \geq 8) = \frac{45}{1024} + \frac{10}{1024} + \frac{1}{1024} = \frac{56}{1024} = \frac{7}{128}
